# Template for a local .env file. Copy it to .env and put real values there: git ignores .env,
# this file is committed and public, so it only ever holds names and placeholders.
#
# The game needs no secrets today. It runs entirely in the player's browser and everything it ships
# (dist/) is readable by anyone. Vite hands variables named VITE_* to the game code, which means
# they end up in the published site: a VITE_ variable must never hold a key, token or password.
# A real secret belongs only to code that runs on a machine you control (tools/, or a server added later),
# read with process.env.NAME after `node --env-file-if-exists=.env tools/<script>.mjs`.
# For the GitHub Pages build, secrets go in GitHub: Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions.
#
# Optional tool settings (not secrets):
# PALUDARIUM_METRICS_DIR=metrics
